// E0003: a multi-character literal like 'AB' is rejected. It used to be
// misdiagnosed as "unterminated" with a machine-applicable autofix that
// inserted a stray quote (turning 'AB' into 'A'B'). The lexer now scans
// for a closing quote to tell a multi-char literal apart from a genuinely
// unterminated one, reports a single clear error, and offers no harmful fix.
![config(testing)]
![config(negative, E0003)]
namespace CryoTests::Negative::MultiCharCharLiteral;
function main() -> int {
    const c: char = 'AB';
    return 0;
}
